The audio input thread deletes its IMPAudio on exit but leaves
global_audio[0]->imp_audio pointing at it. main decides whether there is an
audio thread to stop from that pointer, so after the mic is turned off the
next audio restart (turning it back on) joins a thread that has already been
joined. That is undefined: on T23 it sometimes returns and sometimes blocks
main for good, leaving RTSP stopped, the mic input never recreated and
prudynt unable to stop cleanly ("did not stop, force-killing").

Clear the pointer after the delete, as the T23 shutdown path already does.

diff --git a/src/audio/AudioWorker.cpp b/src/audio/AudioWorker.cpp
index d6f9f77..6ae27d2 100644
--- a/src/audio/AudioWorker.cpp
+++ b/src/audio/AudioWorker.cpp
@@ -527,6 +527,9 @@ void *AudioWorker::thread_entry(void *arg) {
 
   if (global_audio[encChn]->imp_audio) {
     delete global_audio[encChn]->imp_audio;
+    // main joins the audio thread only while imp_audio is set: a stale
+    // pointer makes the next audio restart join this exited thread again.
+    global_audio[encChn]->imp_audio = nullptr;
   }
 
   return 0;
